  "task": "I need to fact-check a citation. This is the citation from the bibliography: Greetham, David. \"Uncoupled: OR, How I Lost My Author(s).\" Textual Cultures: Texts, Contexts, Interpretation, vol. 3 no. 1, 2008, p. 45-46. Project MUSE, doi:10.2979/tex.2008.3.1.44. And this is the in-line citation: Our relationship with the authors of the works we read can often be “obscured not by a \"cloak of print\" but by the veil of scribal confusion and mis-transmission” (Greetham 45-46). Does the quoted text match what is actually in the article? If Yes, answer Yes, otherwise, give me the word in my citation that does not match with the correct one (without any article)."
